{"title":"Hyperbolic trig functions","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The Hyperbolic trig functions can be thought of the classical trig functions except found on an unit hyperbola. There are as follows:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86a0040ffdc0e66486714c9c40d91a4df08b1f69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sinh(x)=\\frac{e^x+e^{-x}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"149\" height=\"36\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16e8b0804278aad185ae2904dad095013b8f44c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cosh(x)=\\frac{e^x-e^{-x}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"151\" height=\"36\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/d/3cdb17648a9a8453851b5021610ad0818a9410e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tanh(x)= \\frac{\\sinh{x}}{\\cosh{x}} =\\frac{e^x+e^{-x}}{e^x-e^{-x}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"229\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>They behave much like normal trig functions, as most of the identities still hold.\nThey do so because:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/a/35afa1ec596c59ff1a98314ea56b27c794d78f84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sinh(x)= -i\\sin{ix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/e/99eb2711be727595211b2dabda6addbfa4bba366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cosh(x)=\\cos{iz}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df03382b6709d62bed6b661fc275b726d85b2a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tanh(x)= -1\\tan{iz}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>However, the arc-hyperbolic trig functions have different derivatives.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Hyperbolic_trig_functions&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018090601\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.012 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 25/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 316/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1210/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.619      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.619      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11926:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018090601 and revision id 231429. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}